  <h1>Best Meat for Beef Jerky</h1>

  <div class="answer-box">
    <p><strong>Best meat for beef jerky:</strong> Eye of round is the top choice — lean, firm, affordable, and slices perfectly. Top round and bottom round are close seconds. All three come from the rear leg, which is low in fat and high in flavor. Avoid fatty cuts like chuck or ribeye — fat goes rancid and shortens shelf life dramatically.</p>
  </div>

